## LAUNCH — Chrome Web Store Submission

### CRITICAL BLOCKERS (must be done before submitting)

- [ ] Set `NEXT_PUBLIC_CHROME_STORE_URL` in production env (currently empty — all CTAs fall back to `#`)
- [ ] Set `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL` to actual domain (currently `elementarmory.example.com` — breaks canonical URLs and OG metadata)
- [ ] Create `/website/public/og-image.png` (1200×630px) — referenced in layout.tsx but missing; breaks social sharing
- [x] Bump extension manifest version from `0.1.0` → `1.0.0` in `chrome-extension/extension/manifest.ts`
- [ ] Create Chrome Web Store listing screenshots (1280×800px, min 1 required — currently none exist)
- [ ] Create Chrome Web Store promotional tile (440×280px small promo image — required for listing)

### Website — Missing Media Assets (launch blockers)

- [ ] Replace all `picsum.photos` placeholder images on homepage (`app/page.tsx`) with real product screenshots
- [ ] Replace all `picsum.photos` placeholder images on product page (`app/product/page.tsx`) with real screenshots
- [ ] Replace all `picsum.photos` placeholder images on features page (`app/features/page.tsx`) with real screenshots
- [ ] Create `/website/public/assets/inline-styles-only.gif` — referenced in `app/page.tsx` but file does not exist
- [ ] Capture/create real screenshots for: capture flow, library view, sync, AI rebuild
- [ ] Create or remove hero visual (Hero component renders `MediaPlaceholder` if no image prop supplied)

### Website — Content & Copy

- [x] Populate or remove the Roadmap page (`app/roadmap/page.tsx`) — currently shows placeholder text "Planned features and improvements will be listed here."
- [ ] Verify `support@elementarmory.com` is live and monitored (appears in Privacy Policy, Terms, and uninstall feedback pages)
- [x] Review all compare pages (`/compare/vs-*`) for accuracy against current feature set
- [x] Audit changelog page — ensure it reflects real shipped versions, not placeholder entries

### Extension — UI & Style Fixes

- [x] Fix preview page editor zoom — `--preview-editor-height` is fixed at `280px` in `preview/styles.css`; the editor pane does not flex or resize with the window, leaving the preview iframe squished on smaller screens
- [x] Tailwind copy button in extension popup returns `<!-- Tailwind conversion coming soon -->` — either implement or hide the button until the feature ships
- [x] Capture count meter in popup — show `used / limit` visual progress bar (currently no quota UI)
- [x] Paywall prompt at limit — currently no in-extension message when quota is reached

### Extension — Quota & Entitlements (MVP enforcement)

- [x] Server-side capture count per install and per user per billing period
- [x] Return `quota_used` and `quota_limit` from `GET /api/billing/entitlement`
- [x] Enforce at capture creation: anonymous over limit → 402 `quota_reached`; free over limit → 402 with upgrade URL; pro → pass

### Infrastructure

- [ ] Configure production environment variables for website deployment
- [ ] Confirm `start.sh` and Docker setup works end-to-end in production
- [ ] Nightly DB backup to S3 with retention policy
- [ ] Basic monitoring / error tracking on server (request logs, health endpoint)
- [ ] Verify extension connects to production API URL (not localhost) in release build

